The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says the ticket is one issue with one fix queued. Its own
table says otherwise: it renders two causes, and a note that some reports are a one-day move.
The subject-line rule ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) merged them,
because every one of these reports says "wrong date" in some words. The fix queued for the
parser does not fix the other two.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 holds three problems. Each now has its own ticket, below. The counts come from the
export at render time; when the desk merges more reports, they change here.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and these tenants write the day
  first. The report says a day and a month swapped, e.g. "1 March is now 3 January". This is the
  fix already queued.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, but reads the date
  the tenant's way, day first. People type what the hint tells them, and the date flips. Only
  reports sent through the form of a booking-v3 tenant. The parser fix does not touch it; the
  form hint (or the form's reading) has to change.
- **`one-day`**: the date moves by one day, not by a swapped month: "Client in Lisbon got
  Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." It looks like a time zone or day-boundary bug. The
  desk already read these as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), but the cause table files them
  under `parser` by tenant.

## How the reports were split

1. One id, one report: the export lists some reports twice.
2. The cause comes from the tenant (locale and booking form) and the channel, as
   `causes.ts` defines it, never from `intakeTag`. Intake guesses from the browser, and its
   guess disagrees with the cause on dozens of these reports.
3. Reports the desk read as a one-day move are their own problem.
4. The subject line decides nothing. Many different subjects were merged into #4471, and one
   subject can belong to any of the three problems.

## The desk's own table, for comparison

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- When a merged ticket's table shows more than one cause, split it before it is marked known.
- Read the rendered page, not only its words: here the table disagreed with the text above it.

